🐛 Bug
If a python dictionary is used in a torchscripted function, calls to dict.update() will fail silently after the first call.
To Reproduce
Steps to reproduce the behavior:
@torch.jit.script
def upd() -> Dict[str, int]:
    a: Dict[str, int] = {}
    for i in range(3):
        a.update({'a': i})
    return a

print(upd())
# > {'a': 0}

